          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Chloe’s annual salary is $72 800.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p45-q20-prompt-change",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Chloe’s employer is increasing her annual salary by 1% but removing the 17.5% leave loading on 4 weeks’ pay.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p45-q20-prompt-comparison",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Is she better or worse off, and by how much?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "She is worse off by \\$252 per year.",
      "worked": "$\\begin{align*}\\text{Weekly pay} &= \\$72\\,800 \\div 52 \\\\ &= \\$1\\,400 \\\\ \\text{Leave loading} &= 0.175 \\times \\$1\\,400 \\times 4 \\\\ &= \\$980 \\\\ \\text{Annual salary increase} &= 0.01 \\times \\$72\\,800 \\\\ &= \\$728 \\\\ \\text{Annual loss} &= \\$980 - \\$728 \\\\ &= \\$252\\end{align*}$\n\nShe is worse off by \\$252 per year because the salary increase is less than the lost leave loading.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
